  "target_rule": "The target is the LATEST qiskit-ibm-runtime release, reached in two layers. HOP A (documented): apply every change whose grounding is a release-note or migration-guide `url`, bringing the code up to the current public API. HOP B (client-side primitives): the eventual destination is the client-side (Executor-backed) SamplerV2/EstimatorV2 in qiskit_ibm_runtime.executor_sampler / executor_estimator, released and documented in 0.50.0 \u2014 which also DEPRECATES the server-side SamplerV2/EstimatorV2 in favor of them. It is grounded in the PUBLISHED migration guide named by the `url` on the `server-to-client` entry (and by `companion_url` on `v1-to-v2`). Always run hop A before hop B, and only attempt hop B when the INSTALLED qiskit-ibm-runtime is >= 0.50.0 (min_runtime_version). State clearly in the plan that hop B is now the recommended destination and that the server-side primitives it replaces are on a deprecation clock.\n",
